[gd_scene load_steps=18 format=3]

; Seabed plant. Replaces an earlier version of this file that was 56 stacked
; BoxMeshes arranged as a staircase of cubes: it read as a blocky green step
; rather than a plant, and cost 56 draw calls per instance across the ~200
; instances in the 16 levels.
;
; Now 16 alpha-blended quads in three height classes -- a low skirt of short
; grass, a main seagrass tuft, and three tall kelp fronds rising through it.
; Every quad has its own yaw, tilt and lean so no two face the same way, and
; all bases sit on y = 0 so the blades emerge from the sand at whatever height
; the level instance places them.
;
; Each class has its own material so the shader's blade_height matches its
; meshes. That uniform normalises the sway falloff, so a wide height spread
; inside a single class would leave the short blades stiff and the tall ones
; barely moving; height variety is carried by the layering instead, and
; silhouette variety by width, yaw, tilt and lean.
;
; Look and motion come from materials/seagrass.tres, materials/seagrass_low.tres
; and materials/kelp_frond.tres; see shaders/seagrass.gdshader for the
; world-space sway and how these are blended.

[ext_resource type="Material" path="res://materials/seagrass.tres" id="1_tuft"]
[ext_resource type="Material" path="res://materials/seagrass_low.tres" id="2_low"]
[ext_resource type="Material" path="res://materials/kelp_frond.tres" id="3_frond"]

